#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186657680 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35aba803-7e19-5f64-ae12-70549369c0c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{(8x+2)^{3}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657664}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186657664} :answer-field/id #uuid "114eabe9-88a9-521f-991b-55f2cc647709" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657659}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e61f263e-2780-5a15-b73e-edd6546f8ecb" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8x+2}}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=8x+2.$ Then $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}={u}^{-1/2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=-\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{-3/2}=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=8.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{(8x+2)^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186657682 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00ad8cba-4c43-5466-991c-8f58f1b2c414" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{-7x-6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657657} {:answer/id #uuid "31e7578d-8b52-580a-afa3-98f20764e7e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{-7x-6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657662} {:answer/id #uuid "6da4c05a-424b-5485-beff-b0b4d9364431" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{2\\sqrt{-7x-6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657667} {:answer/id #uuid "856b17f1-3e5d-5e34-99a4-069fedec4af0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{-7x-6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657672} {:answer/id #uuid "96693fb7-81ed-5735-a956-5196bd2f34a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{-7x-6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657675}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186657662} :answer-field/id #uuid "02bdd7f6-dc11-5437-83b6-6f0871573543" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657658}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f48647ea-8ebd-5583-b713-aef1cac5a291" :question/problem "Given that $y=\\sqrt{-6-7x},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "We use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=-6-7x.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}={u}^{1/2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{-1/2}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-7.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (-7) \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{-6-7x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671807 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a07cfb7-4cad-58e0-a4d0-e4f2d278150e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671812} {:answer/id #uuid "7b9963be-748b-59d9-b232-408c08579748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x+1)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671815} {:answer/id #uuid "9868d3e4-f7cb-57e8-9301-8d3315ab32af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671818} {:answer/id #uuid "bea06560-306b-5191-b859-68a659a93574" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671828} {:answer/id #uuid "e9f6a50b-aa05-5c4d-949f-3b6cec8c570b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x+1}{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671832}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671828} :answer-field/id #uuid "1efeba55-84f5-5363-86b8-c3a17d7c4c46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671806}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1f3824b9-c900-5e9e-8087-0cc8093edc0c" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x{y}^{3}}{x+1}\n$$\n\nWork on a domain where all displayed expressions are defined." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differential equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(\\frac{x}{x+1})\\cdot {y}^{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{x+1}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671808 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "146a6848-4c14-54f4-896c-6353d2be975f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671804} {:answer/id #uuid "1dddfec0-8c43-5725-82f4-bf621478bf25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671805} {:answer/id #uuid "4541b76c-c7b3-5127-b1e4-c58c64357eda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{4}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671811} {:answer/id #uuid "87cff2c1-2f5f-5115-a5f6-9a13401b251c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡5x}{{y}^{4}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671816} {:answer/id #uuid "b147539d-7371-5abc-b988-808f480064ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡5x\\text{ }\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671823}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671811} :answer-field/id #uuid "d38167bd-5604-5321-bf6c-b37cfdaa0c84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671830}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2b2de01b-9c24-57b5-ab7b-9a58a2d499df" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\n$$\n\nWork on a domain where all displayed expressions are defined." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differential equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\cdot {y}^{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{y}^{4}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671809 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0901fe67-23ab-5ba3-b592-df465e6d58e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={4}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671803} {:answer/id #uuid "ad252bce-54c5-5a83-8785-c5467955fd75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={4}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671819} {:answer/id #uuid "afc8ebe3-8b39-563f-bdd1-f323a95cd07c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={4}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671822} {:answer/id #uuid "b6e6007a-9a24-555e-9508-27bd11306b95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={4}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671824} {:answer/id #uuid "ec8f5c3a-726a-570d-9b70-c29708c1834b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={4}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671833}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671824} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2ba0e5c-3850-5567-9b1b-5e8d4197744e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671835}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3d2da0ff-f35d-57a2-b6bc-f73ea32ee54e" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{4}^{4x}}{{y}^{4}}\n$$\n\nWork on a domain where all displayed expressions are defined." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differential equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={4}^{4x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{y}^{4}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n{y}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={4}^{4x}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671836 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b4f35d9-488b-510e-ae8b-c7bdec3e214e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x+2}{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671814} {:answer/id #uuid "927d7c9c-7c88-56a4-bb96-9228be003e59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671817} {:answer/id #uuid "b7637471-17ff-5dac-a428-f7ea2286d7ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671825} {:answer/id #uuid "d1482077-a0ab-5428-be6c-a6547a3e99ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671829} {:answer/id #uuid "f206f8f0-1ba0-5b8b-bf32-f65a750f7264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x+2)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671834}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671817} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae41734e-ef85-5b0c-a7c5-8ec5da72ddb3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671821}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f53921ad-14e5-53c4-8aac-ee2f62ff5e14" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x{y}^{3}}{x+2}\n$$\n\nWork on a domain where all displayed expressions are defined." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differential equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(\\frac{x}{x+2})\\cdot {y}^{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{x+2}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671837 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44b2395c-9177-5c71-93ce-21b5d23bcaf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{4x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671810} {:answer/id #uuid "59cc5e7d-45cc-5682-9aeb-9c114937332e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671813} {:answer/id #uuid "ad6a02c2-84cf-5126-98e5-1c572aca6d39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-4x}}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671820} {:answer/id #uuid "bb74df3e-88fa-5a64-8607-b7f384c999a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671827} {:answer/id #uuid "da90372f-d502-52aa-84c2-46e0cfb2eb5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{-4x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671831}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671813} :answer-field/id #uuid "b891c151-dbc1-5e86-a54a-094aae5b0b52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671826}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f7f03e26-82e0-5fd2-a240-4632479a76e4" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y{e}^{4x}\n$$\n\nWork on a domain where all displayed expressions are defined." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differential equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{4x}\\cdot y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{4x}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671842 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08259c26-cd01-57fc-8bd4-97710fe61f79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\left(C + 3 \\left(x + 7\\right)^{2}\\right)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671841} {:answer/id #uuid "389dcd83-3be6-5ae7-8536-11e51af3d592" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\left(C + \\left(x + 7\\right)^{2}\\right)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671847} {:answer/id #uuid "4cc19ee9-085a-53a3-9ebd-784a3aa3752f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\left(C - \\left(x + 7\\right)^{2}\\right)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671849} {:answer/id #uuid "91cc18a4-7ab7-5560-9d49-5e0a4fc0d29c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\left(C - 2 \\left(x + 7\\right)^{2}\\right)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671864} {:answer/id #uuid "ba88b057-eed7-5cc6-bd3a-e13e9089e059" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\left(C + 2 \\left(x + 7\\right)^{2}\\right)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671868}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671847} :answer-field/id #uuid "d446d84a-f723-5bc5-9258-11f27b7d620c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671871}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1b625cbe-e98e-52a2-876f-b8846d653bd3" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y′=\\left(6 x + 42\\right)\\sqrt[3]{y^2}.$ Work on intervals where $y\\ne 0$; cube roots are real." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y′ & =\\left(6 x + 42\\right)\\sqrt[3]{y^2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{y^2}}\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =2 x + 14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{y^2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\int 2 x + 14\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{y} & =\\left(x + 7\\right)^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution in implicit form is\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{y}=\\left(x + 7\\right)^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ Solving for $y$ gives\n\n$$\ny=\\left(C + \\left(x + 7\\right)^{2}\\right)^{3}.\n$$\n\nHere $C$ is an arbitrary real constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671846 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1efe4088-e51b-5797-a073-9e5ef1be0ff5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{C + 2 \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671844} {:answer/id #uuid "7de0ecca-e5d6-59cb-8703-a77d18534315" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{C - \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671859} {:answer/id #uuid "8563ce9a-2222-580d-a85a-03e7321d082a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{C - 2 \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671860} {:answer/id #uuid "9a2f0086-02ae-5d62-b506-2977900faf52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{C + \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671865} {:answer/id #uuid "de910995-243e-53a6-b31f-d50546e6b6dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{C + 3 \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671872}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671872} :answer-field/id #uuid "60de23b9-01a7-5c81-a3ec-22524e07f3e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671853}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "349ca8c0-aa18-5536-91e2-5228615e320b" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y′=\\frac{6 x - 12}{3 y^{2}}.$ Work on intervals where $y\\ne 0$; cube roots are real." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y′ & =\\frac{6 x - 12}{3 y^{2}} \\\\ 3 y^{2}\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =6 x - 12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3 y^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\int 6 x - 12\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ y^{3} & =3 \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution in implicit form is\n\n$$\ny^{3}=3 \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ Solving for $y$ gives\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt[3]{C + 3 \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nHere $C$ is an arbitrary real constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671850 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "031a129f-52d6-5681-914e-7769e63f4f73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\ln{\\left(C + \\left(x - 8\\right)^{2} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671840} {:answer/id #uuid "66f1a978-e987-5bc7-8d12-bb049ca62af8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\ln{\\left(C + \\frac{\\left(x - 8\\right)^{2}}{2} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671855} {:answer/id #uuid "6a024c65-98cf-5df3-a7c1-9fef172fd026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\ln{\\left(C - \\frac{\\left(x - 8\\right)^{2}}{2} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671856} {:answer/id #uuid "90385026-40d1-5b70-9910-305c6baa74f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\ln{\\left(C + \\frac{3 \\left(x - 8\\right)^{2}}{2} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671863} {:answer/id #uuid "b00f57f9-5b2b-5444-9f23-46a31d7ebdbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\ln{\\left(C - \\left(x - 8\\right)^{2} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671867}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671855} :answer-field/id #uuid "263632f2-df73-5f67-9e44-f172ab629be2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671845}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4e2e674b-0850-5368-88f6-14e03d6bfda5" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y′=\\left(x - 8\\right) e^{- y}.$ Work on intervals where the logarithm argument is positive." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y′ & =\\left(x - 8\\right) e^{- y} \\\\ e^{y}\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =x - 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int e^{y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\int x - 8\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ e^{y} & =\\frac{\\left(x - 8\\right)^{2}}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution in implicit form is\n\n$$\ne^{y}=\\frac{\\left(x - 8\\right)^{2}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ Solving for $y$ gives\n\n$$\ny=\\ln{\\left(C + \\frac{\\left(x - 8\\right)^{2}}{2} \\right)}.\n$$\n\nHere $C$ is an arbitrary real constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671852 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40de40ea-de47-5945-83e5-48552756376d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{C + 3 \\left(x + 4\\right)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671848} {:answer/id #uuid "6c337c3f-e451-5f2b-8028-cc25f22de1ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{C - \\left(x + 4\\right)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671857} {:answer/id #uuid "7c3af1fe-7854-5d59-8d54-20802f3b93c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{C + \\left(x + 4\\right)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671858} {:answer/id #uuid "c676eb7d-d036-56b0-9476-a8bc8f71b959" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{C - 2 \\left(x + 4\\right)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671870} {:answer/id #uuid "fbc6ce09-69ed-5a62-9eb1-12cde5e864b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{C + 2 \\left(x + 4\\right)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671873}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671870} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cb0fb69-bacc-5d3c-a375-f02460cca2ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "56a509c2-c05b-5e8a-a692-10fa903b3237" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y′=\\frac{- 4 x - 16}{3 y^{2}}.$ Work on intervals where $y\\ne 0$; cube roots are real." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y′ & =\\frac{- 4 x - 16}{3 y^{2}} \\\\ 3 y^{2}\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =- 4 x - 16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3 y^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\int - 4 x - 16\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ y^{3} & =- 2 \\left(x + 4\\right)^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution in implicit form is\n\n$$\ny^{3}=- 2 \\left(x + 4\\right)^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ Solving for $y$ gives\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt[3]{C - 2 \\left(x + 4\\right)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nHere $C$ is an arbitrary real constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671866 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0290a6d7-2380-5108-8789-71bfb77109ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{C + 2 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671839} {:answer/id #uuid "4ed6957e-4f4f-56e4-b4ca-d10746070f85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{C - x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671851} {:answer/id #uuid "623c0c49-9e21-57ef-89e7-a97e9e53c353" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{C - 2 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671854} {:answer/id #uuid "85b3ccab-157b-52d4-ad5b-5ceacfd368dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{C + x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671861} {:answer/id #uuid "8d322dc8-4070-5f87-8b51-bfa4b0de44ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{C + 3 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671862}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671854} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb033a9e-00be-5d83-9371-6ce820188add" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671869}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a959a07a-ae37-59fb-85ec-1a2785aa394a" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y′=- \\frac{4 x}{3 y^{2}}.$ Work on intervals where $y\\ne 0$; cube roots are real." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y′ & =- \\frac{4 x}{3 y^{2}} \\\\ 3 y^{2}\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =- 4 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3 y^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\int - 4 x\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ y^{3} & =- 2 x^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution in implicit form is\n\n$$\ny^{3}=- 2 x^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ Solving for $y$ gives\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt[3]{C - 2 x^{2}}.\n$$\n\nHere $C$ is an arbitrary real constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671882 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d1f9dec-ea36-5760-aa71-a248fe6858cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\tan{\\left(y - 1 \\right)}=- 2 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671884} {:answer/id #uuid "5b80337c-a8d8-5954-881a-6e30c779219c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\tan{\\left(y - 1 \\right)}=3 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671885} {:answer/id #uuid "6f91dfad-227a-50ff-8d6f-06a3c27249b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\tan{\\left(y - 1 \\right)}=2 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671890} {:answer/id #uuid "cb2c70e7-64db-5ac9-8a8a-7385d1eaa8d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\tan{\\left(y - 1 \\right)}=- x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671902} {:answer/id #uuid "fb797a13-a6ea-58d1-8b4b-aeb7938f3880" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\tan{\\left(y - 1 \\right)}=x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671909}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671890} :answer-field/id #uuid "60fd060d-b7e8-5351-be92-90bb8b43d43a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671886}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "461967d1-8106-5690-8e41-619893730384" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2 \\cos^{2}{\\left(y - 1 \\right)}$ for $$\n\\displaystyle -\\frac{\\pi }{2}<\\left(y-1\\right)<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 \\cos^{2}{\\left(y - 1 \\right)} \\\\ (\\sec^{2}{\\left(y - 1 \\right)})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\sec^{2}{\\left(y - 1 \\right)})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\sec^{2}{\\left(y - 1 \\right)})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int (2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\sec^{2}{\\left(y - 1 \\right)})\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\tan{\\left(y - 1 \\right)} & =2 x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\tan{\\left(y - 1 \\right)}=2 x+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671896 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "297b530e-20d7-5e81-b425-fa1768707754" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(y - 6\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}=- 2 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671877} {:answer/id #uuid "3b0ca276-9e95-579e-8f2a-a9c6b5a9df45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(y - 6\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}=3 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671879} {:answer/id #uuid "458ec8b8-a147-5276-9b8b-caafcc4876ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(y - 6\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}=2 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671881} {:answer/id #uuid "6310a5d0-5e6e-58a0-9e28-f8ce43f9ddda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(y - 6\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}=\\left(x - 3\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671887} {:answer/id #uuid "f9a2174b-195b-5b75-a33b-e70cd25e9c31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(y - 6\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}=- \\left(x - 3\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671908}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671881} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6c7faae-0ae2-5a40-8884-ddbd1ec282c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671901}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8bf38184-71b3-55e0-aae7-92ac2d3b9083" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2 \\sqrt{x - 3}}{\\sqrt{y - 6}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2 \\sqrt{x - 3}}{\\sqrt{y - 6}} \\\\ (\\sqrt{y - 6})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 \\sqrt{x - 3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\sqrt{y - 6})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2 \\sqrt{x - 3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\sqrt{y - 6})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int (2 \\sqrt{x - 3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\sqrt{y - 6})\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (2 \\sqrt{x - 3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{2 \\left(y - 6\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3} & =\\frac{4 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}+K \\\\ \\left(y - 6\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}} & =2 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=\\frac{3}{2}K.$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\left(y - 6\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}=2 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671899 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4681cc65-906b-5c53-8969-874b8ec69174" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\arcsin{\\left(y - 3 \\right)}=2 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671883} {:answer/id #uuid "742f05d3-92c4-5aa5-8c41-93e519ebc1c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\arcsin{\\left(y - 3 \\right)}=3 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671892} {:answer/id #uuid "7501d289-566e-5a66-9f8e-ccd217907c39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\arcsin{\\left(y - 3 \\right)}=x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671893} {:answer/id #uuid "77812baa-ca7f-51ec-8b26-1968eba43ddb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\arcsin{\\left(y - 3 \\right)}=- 2 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671894} {:answer/id #uuid "edb66c36-2956-5340-9b17-714a9784e244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\arcsin{\\left(y - 3 \\right)}=- x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671906}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671893} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bef3a4e-4f48-5971-9dee-e2d365a8e974" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "98eb94b6-6c49-5a95-aced-95c12633a495" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{1 - \\left(y - 3\\right)^{2}}$ for $\\,|\\left(y-3\\right)|<1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\sqrt{1 - \\left(y - 3\\right)^{2}} \\\\ (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - \\left(y - 3\\right)^{2}}})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - \\left(y - 3\\right)^{2}}})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - \\left(y - 3\\right)^{2}}})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int (1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - \\left(y - 3\\right)^{2}}})\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\arcsin{\\left(y - 3 \\right)} & =x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\arcsin{\\left(y - 3 \\right)}=x+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671904 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e08556e-fe3a-5878-b374-961b439e063d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{y + 4}=- \\left(x - 3\\right)^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671875} {:answer/id #uuid "4029d02d-b992-5899-80f5-2554751a5818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{y + 4}=3 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671880} {:answer/id #uuid "8eb864ea-b06f-5970-b44a-e0cf169dfad2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{y + 4}=\\left(x - 3\\right)^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671897} {:answer/id #uuid "9cf932c7-9c4b-5af3-a737-4a19ffa61c19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{y + 4}=- 2 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671900} {:answer/id #uuid "d7e71904-5acc-5fa1-91a1-acb20f519d18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{y + 4}=2 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671903}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671900} :answer-field/id #uuid "f08142dc-d542-59d8-b38e-e6dccfcfe24b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671907}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e2cf29a2-5dd5-58a3-9067-e59917e63171" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\left(12 - 4 x\\right) e^{- y - 4}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\left(12 - 4 x\\right) e^{- y - 4} \\\\ (e^{y + 4})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =12 - 4 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (e^{y + 4})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (12 - 4 x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (e^{y + 4})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int (12 - 4 x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (e^{y + 4})\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (12 - 4 x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ e^{y + 4} & =- 2 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\ne^{y + 4}=- 2 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{2}+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671905 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26137cb8-e918-5ce9-b1fb-a49224f742d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{y - 2}=- \\left(x + 5\\right)^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671876} {:answer/id #uuid "34dbabbc-15c2-56c3-b7ec-71ccc050174d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{y - 2}=2 \\left(x + 5\\right)^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671878} {:answer/id #uuid "65613dad-adcb-552f-b5c3-f9dacd4d0a12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{y - 2}=- 2 \\left(x + 5\\right)^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671888} {:answer/id #uuid "6dd9c0c9-ec62-516b-85fe-3b2ec0a8b6f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{y - 2}=3 \\left(x + 5\\right)^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671889} {:answer/id #uuid "6fe7436e-4be6-500c-9475-57df72c68a31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{y - 2}=\\left(x + 5\\right)^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671891}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671878} :answer-field/id #uuid "95c14b72-7237-51b9-8103-a1ca772f4105" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e414420b-974e-5702-bd35-607d710c9d38" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\left(4 x + 20\\right) e^{2 - y}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\left(4 x + 20\\right) e^{2 - y} \\\\ (e^{y - 2})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4 x + 20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (e^{y - 2})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4 x + 20)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (e^{y - 2})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int (4 x + 20)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (e^{y - 2})\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (4 x + 20)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ e^{y - 2} & =2 \\left(x + 5\\right)^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\ne^{y - 2}=2 \\left(x + 5\\right)^{2}+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671917 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ee20c7f-6f9d-58e0-86be-a21e4c190232" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K - 6 x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671916} {:answer/id #uuid "314ddc43-96f1-59a8-8023-3bb59824bbd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{- 12 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671918} {:answer/id #uuid "3cd63917-a749-555a-bf9d-2fac66925065" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{- 6 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671919} {:answer/id #uuid "43728ce3-eb2b-5fc6-830f-805a4c28dae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K + e^{- 6 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671921} {:answer/id #uuid "504849f0-11de-50f0-9d0f-349aab8ada59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{6 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671923}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671919} :answer-field/id #uuid "0984a0b2-b439-5c38-8752-ca7940686554" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671911}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2979f6cd-5c5b-5031-9aef-e33515fe3ba1" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y'+12 xy=0$ for $y\\ne0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'+12 xy=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+12 xy & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- 12 xy \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- 12 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (- 12 x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (- 12 x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\ln|y| & =- 6 x^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln|y|=- 6 x^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln|y| & =- 6 x^{2}+C \\\\ |y| & =e^{- 6 x^{2}+C} \\\\ |y| & =e^{- 6 x^{2}}\\cdot e^C \\\\ |y| & =K e^{- 6 x^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=e^C$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K e^{- 6 x^{2}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671922 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11f9cf16-55c7-5532-a0f0-23f1210aa4a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K + e^{2 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671914} {:answer/id #uuid "3d01e966-51d4-5f5f-999e-14a3d35823f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{2 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671920} {:answer/id #uuid "8493af28-b3ab-5643-8356-07d1df783a26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{4 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671927} {:answer/id #uuid "eefa0af9-582a-593c-b08c-680c52172c6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K + 2 x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671941} {:answer/id #uuid "f2393c7a-c3d8-5aad-bed7-a830f13b0967" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{- 2 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671943}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671920} :answer-field/id #uuid "c218409c-26c1-5438-adf5-477c4d837748" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671936}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4a1b84c2-72ff-5b6c-a2d3-124405d3d5d9" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y'-4 xy=0$ for $y\\ne0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'-4 xy=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4 xy & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4 xy \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4 x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (4 x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\ln|y| & =2 x^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln|y|=2 x^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln|y| & =2 x^{2}+C \\\\ |y| & =e^{2 x^{2}+C} \\\\ |y| & =e^{2 x^{2}}\\cdot e^C \\\\ |y| & =K e^{2 x^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=e^C$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K e^{2 x^{2}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671925 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10613b20-4546-5c4a-aa07-4879beaa6a0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K - \\frac{x^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671912} {:answer/id #uuid "56ae88cd-afef-5b6b-abda-e32d3d00029b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671924} {:answer/id #uuid "a065ca85-23b9-57a2-9c4f-19506037b638" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671930} {:answer/id #uuid "a9e0e78d-dfa5-5ef8-a0a3-a891d60b5f3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671932} {:answer/id #uuid "d56f3b88-010b-54af-b551-06716606f0b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K + e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671937}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671932} :answer-field/id #uuid "10cb28d7-d622-5eda-905c-fd0e046fd019" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671913}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "63d7f230-b140-54c5-82dd-72d37987d264" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y'+xy=0$ for $y\\ne0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'+xy=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+xy & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- xy \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (- x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (- x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\ln|y| & =- \\frac{x^{2}}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln|y|=- \\frac{x^{2}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln|y| & =- \\frac{x^{2}}{2}+C \\\\ |y| & =e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{2}+C} \\\\ |y| & =e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{2}}\\cdot e^C \\\\ |y| & =K e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=e^C$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{2}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671926 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9111a873-e65b-50bf-bdd6-54909ccca12a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K + e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671929} {:answer/id #uuid "b118235d-1829-5423-8043-a5f080f66a52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K + \\frac{x^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671934} {:answer/id #uuid "dc36d5d0-64d5-5ada-8fb7-841e9841e414" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671938} {:answer/id #uuid "fbe8bee5-4fc4-5696-a87a-7c22a9798075" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671944} {:answer/id #uuid "fcabaf0c-d3ac-5e0a-ae3b-aa11ef9021e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671945}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671945} :answer-field/id #uuid "1763bee1-cfb8-5a3e-9de0-c430dd931519" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671915}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "673675bd-5c68-5cda-a7b2-bd4261ad478c" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y'-xy=0$ for $y\\ne0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'-xy=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-xy & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =xy \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\ln|y| & =\\frac{x^{2}}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln|y|=\\frac{x^{2}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln|y| & =\\frac{x^{2}}{2}+C \\\\ |y| & =e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{2}+C} \\\\ |y| & =e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{2}}\\cdot e^C \\\\ |y| & =K e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=e^C$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{2}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671935 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85fb30b9-482c-5836-b259-f18647c2ac3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K + e^{- \\frac{3 x^{2}}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671928} {:answer/id #uuid "ab4eed85-3711-57b4-9b07-9168e188a322" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{\\frac{3 x^{2}}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671933} {:answer/id #uuid "e054d655-62a4-5394-ac47-ef25847f1064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K - \\frac{3 x^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671939} {:answer/id #uuid "e5e7cc48-efe1-565e-a021-4a7d3578b2f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{- \\frac{3 x^{2}}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671940} {:answer/id #uuid "efb430f8-926e-55a9-90f2-160fd4d71619" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{- 3 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671942}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671940} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5b85e77-d6a2-593a-bb62-e1913ab6c0ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671931}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b6e881a1-d03e-538b-b25f-9901e5967e80" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y'+3 xy=0$ for $y\\ne0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'+3 xy=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3 xy & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- 3 xy \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- 3 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (- 3 x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (- 3 x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\ln|y| & =- \\frac{3 x^{2}}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln|y|=- \\frac{3 x^{2}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln|y| & =- \\frac{3 x^{2}}{2}+C \\\\ |y| & =e^{- \\frac{3 x^{2}}{2}+C} \\\\ |y| & =e^{- \\frac{3 x^{2}}{2}}\\cdot e^C \\\\ |y| & =K e^{- \\frac{3 x^{2}}{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=e^C$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K e^{- \\frac{3 x^{2}}{2}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672493 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e01c205-50bc-5b38-bb49-500a06736b9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{(x + 2)}+2{(x + 2)}^{2}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672497}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672497} :answer-field/id #uuid "9260f8a1-641f-53e5-bfac-d94a2cad0c72" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672501}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1d2a9b12-3282-565d-8e04-5064a23ae3d7" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\sqrt{(x + 2)}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4(x + 2)\\sqrt{(x + 2)}=3$ that satisfies $y(-1)=11.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(x + 2)}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4(x + 2)\\sqrt{(x + 2)} & =3 \\\\ \\sqrt{(x + 2)}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3+4(x + 2)\\sqrt{(x + 2)} \\\\ \\text{d}y & =(3{(x + 2)}^{-1/2}+4(x + 2))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\text{d}y & =\\int (3{(x + 2)}^{-1/2}+4(x + 2))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =6{(x + 2)}^{1/2}+2{(x + 2)}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(-1)=11$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(-1) & =11 \\\\ 6(1)^{1/2}+2(1)^{2}+C & =11 \\\\ C+8 & =11 \\\\ C & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =6{(x + 2)}^{1/2}+2{(x + 2)}^{2}+3 \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{(x + 2)}+2{(x + 2)}^{2}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672494 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d059536-0109-5359-8442-84b64e83fc4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{(x - 3)}+4{(x - 3)}^{2}+7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672496}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672496} :answer-field/id #uuid "c26ba58a-d6c3-5eca-8d6a-deb9c0b2c874" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672506}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3a0761a3-71cc-54d6-bed4-7a048e3a0e98" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${(x - 3)}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8{(x - 3)}^{3}=5$ that satisfies $y(4)=6.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x - 3)}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8{(x - 3)}^{3} & =5 \\\\ {(x - 3)}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5+8{(x - 3)}^{3} \\\\ \\text{d}y & =(5{(x - 3)}^{-2}+8(x - 3))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\text{d}y & =\\int (5{(x - 3)}^{-2}+8(x - 3))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-5{(x - 3)}^{-1}+4{(x - 3)}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(4)=6$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(4) & =6 \\\\ -5(1)^{-1}+4(1)^{2}+C & =6 \\\\ C-1 & =6 \\\\ C & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =-5{(x - 3)}^{-1}+4{(x - 3)}^{2}+7 \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{(x - 3)}+4{(x - 3)}^{2}+7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672499 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c8df881-79fc-597e-905f-47b603e8fcc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{(x + 3)}+4{(x + 3)}^{2}+7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672495}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672495} :answer-field/id #uuid "9933f373-e852-5e58-920e-b22d113465ab" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672503}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6f76f884-1ea4-506a-b48f-3d11fe42414b" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${(x + 3)}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8{(x + 3)}^{3}=5$ that satisfies $y(-2)=6.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x + 3)}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8{(x + 3)}^{3} & =5 \\\\ {(x + 3)}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5+8{(x + 3)}^{3} \\\\ \\text{d}y & =(5{(x + 3)}^{-2}+8(x + 3))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\text{d}y & =\\int (5{(x + 3)}^{-2}+8(x + 3))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-5{(x + 3)}^{-1}+4{(x + 3)}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(-2)=6$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(-2) & =6 \\\\ -5(1)^{-1}+4(1)^{2}+C & =6 \\\\ C-1 & =6 \\\\ C & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =-5{(x + 3)}^{-1}+4{(x + 3)}^{2}+7 \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{(x + 3)}+4{(x + 3)}^{2}+7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672500 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ae6cdd8-7ece-5bb6-a811-74370a2ba5c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}(\\frac{5}{4}-{e}^{-(x - 1)})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672498}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672498} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cdf3e68-d4de-5ad4-9574-fd9a9450108d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672492}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8cebb048-16ac-5152-999b-c80ad00cf72f" :question/problem "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-(x - 1)-y}$ given that $\\,y(1)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-(x - 1)-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-(x - 1)}{e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-(x - 1)} \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{-(x - 1)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{-(x - 1)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & =-{e}^{-(x - 1)}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-(x - 1)}+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-(x - 1)}+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(1)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{0}+C) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-1) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ C-1 & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ C & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-(x - 1)-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{4}-{e}^{-(x - 1)}).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672504 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94ce7cc9-b816-56b4-ac94-13a4ea203437" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x - 3)^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672502}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672502} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2736e4d-28a3-5b77-ae75-c0817ba05432" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672505}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a5b2a220-0459-5dce-b547-6284c446511b" :question/problem "Find the nonconstant local solution to $y'=2(x - 3)\\sqrt{1-y^2}$ by separating variables. Work on a local branch where the sine argument $\\theta$ satisfies $-\\pi/2<\\theta<\\pi/2$. Express the solution as $y=\\sin(\\boxed{\\text{expression}}+C)$.\n\nExpression: {{field-1}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "First, we separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2(x - 3)\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2(x - 3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2(x - 3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y & ={(x - 3)}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a perfectly valid general solution. However, if we want to write $y=y(x)$ explicitly, then we can solve for $y.$ This gives\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({(x - 3)}^{2}+C)\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThis nonconstant branch applies where $-\\pi/2<(x - 3)^2+C<\\pi/2$, so $\\cos((x - 3)^2+C)>0$. The constant endpoint solutions $y=\\pm1$ also solve the ODE."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672548 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bb9aec7-3fe0-5379-b3be-a5cced948ca5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k(N-58)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672544} {:answer/id #uuid "4988d6b2-6cc8-58b8-937b-37187a3c0ccd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k(N-95)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672555} {:answer/id #uuid "5651368d-8257-5fa4-83ce-3bee80076ba4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k(95-N)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672558} {:answer/id #uuid "e0e7cb22-1ac3-5509-bcc5-5a8cd2ed8e7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=-k(58+N)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672573} {:answer/id #uuid "fd8932f3-6f63-564d-8f3a-a114cb7b2c2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k(58-N)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672578}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672558} :answer-field/id #uuid "22b51cd9-5343-564b-8294-8af293032250" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672546}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2667e815-917c-5f12-9c28-0d9309162349" :question/problem "A wildlife manager noted that the growth of the number of deer in a protected forest is directly proportional to the difference between the forest’s maximum deer population and the current population. Let $N(t)$ be the deer population, measured in number of deer, and let $t\\ge 0$ be the time in years. If the maximum deer population that the forest can support is $95$ deer, which differential equation could be used to model the forest’s deer population? Assume that $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality." :question/worked-solution "The rate at which the deer population $N(t)$ of the forest changes is proportional to the difference between the maximum deer population the forest can support and the current deer population. Therefore, we have the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k(a-N),\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the maximum deer population the forest can support, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, $a=95\\text{ deer},$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k(95-N).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672549 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "308cfbc3-831a-5173-a5c5-642d4518abf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=k(P-34)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672550} {:answer/id #uuid "32deb58f-2a4b-5c2c-883c-3c0b907a77ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=-k(34+P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672552} {:answer/id #uuid "88812519-c775-5836-85bb-df3d56d55c46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=k(79-P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672563} {:answer/id #uuid "cc7bb81f-16ec-5b16-aeff-f352e138bc9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=k(34-P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672570} {:answer/id #uuid "e5eb74f9-313b-5dda-b150-454e5979e820" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=k(P-79)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672574}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672570} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4787f96-44e5-5fbd-b936-b744f4936b4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672571}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2be35662-b24d-5c89-874e-5c3591e8d395" :question/problem "A factory's management noted that the growth of the unit production is directly proportional to the difference between the maximum number of units a factory worker can produce and the current production quantity. Let $P(t)$ be the production quantity, measured in units produced, and let $t\\ge 0$ be the time in days. If the maximum number of units that a worker can produce is $34$ $\\text{units}$, which differential equation could be used to model the factory's production? Assume that $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality." :question/worked-solution "The rate at which the production $P(t)$ of the factory changes is proportional to the difference between the maximum number of units a factory worker can produce and the current production quantity. Therefore, we have the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=k(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the maximum number of units a factory worker can produce, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, $a=34\\text{ units},$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=k(34-P).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672551 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24b00dff-c445-5900-a662-fe0a4bb25dac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}F}{\\text{d}t}=k(F-232)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672547} {:answer/id #uuid "434deb99-4c7c-5e2c-bba0-441d1fd87280" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}F}{\\text{d}t}=k(500-F)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672554} {:answer/id #uuid "62be25f4-6c92-5029-9fd7-2d48fc78b642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}F}{\\text{d}t}=k(232-F)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672559} {:answer/id #uuid "64cf5db9-97c0-5548-a365-871a5ee69240" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}F}{\\text{d}t}=kF(500-F)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672560} {:answer/id #uuid "7d660e6c-0b52-5121-912a-d0c481d8d62e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}F}{\\text{d}t}=k(F-500)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672561}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672559} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed5fafe2-a4fe-5096-b57d-62e35de2b3cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672575}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "322e7971-29aa-50c5-a6d3-ea7d6622a62d" :question/problem "An ecologist found that the growth of the number of frogs in a wetland is directly proportional to the difference between the wetland’s maximum frog population and the current population. Let $F(t)$ be the frog population, measured in number of frogs, and let $t\\ge 0$ be the time in years. If the maximum frog population the wetland can support is $232$ frogs, which differential equation could be used to model the frog population? Assume that $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality." :question/worked-solution "The rate at which the frog population $F(t)$ of the wetland changes is proportional to the difference between the maximum frog population the wetland can support and the current frog population. Therefore, we have the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}F}{\\text{d}t}=k(a-F),\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the maximum frog population the wetland can support, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, $a=232\\text{ frogs},$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}F}{\\text{d}t}=k(232-F).\n$$"}]}
